# Build context excludes. Anything here is invisible to `langgraph build` / `langgraph deploy`,
# which build from the WORKING TREE - so this file is the only thing standing between a
# developer's local secrets and an image layer.

# --- secrets, first and non-negotiable ---
# Safe to exclude even though langgraph.json points `env` at .env: the CLI reads that file
# LOCALLY and sends its values to the control plane as deployment secrets
# (langgraph_cli/deploy.py:_secrets_from_env). The image never needs it, and a
# GitHub-integration build never had it anyway, since .env is gitignored.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
token.json

# --- build noise ---
frontend
chat-langchain-lite
.git
.claude
node_modules
**/node_modules
.venv
**/__pycache__
*.log
dist
.DS_Store
